comment_data.body:
free_option_prepared() takes a `const optset_T *`, so it can't clear `os_prepared.ptr` after freeing it. It's safe only if every caller calls it exactly once (which is currently true).

suggestion:

Drop the `const` and clear both fields after freeing, so a second call is harmless:

    void free_option_prepared(optset_T *args)
    {
      if (args->os_prepared_free != NULL && args->os_prepared.ptr != NULL) {
        args->os_prepared_free(args->os_prepared.ptr);
      }
      args->os_prepared.ptr = NULL;
      args->os_prepared_free = NULL;
    }

